&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The EMEA Payroll Analyst role is an operational role designed to provide leading payroll and vendor management services support to Sony Interactive Entertainment. This role is positioned within the People Experience team within HR. You will be responsible for working with external payroll vendor partnership(s), payroll operations and execution, and supporting the production of accurate and timely payroll results across EMEA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relationship Management:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide exceptional experiences, resulting in high customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise between outsource provider and functional staff to bring issues to resolution within provided service level agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with HR, Compensation, Benefits, Finance and other departments to ensure seamless integration of payroll processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with internal partners regarding payroll policies, changes, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payroll Services:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the outsource payroll service provider to ensure delivery of the payroll processes and results&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the preparation and processing of payroll for all employees, ensuring accuracy and compliance with internal policies and legal regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and validate payroll data and ensure timely submission to the payroll vendor, reviewing outputs in line with payroll calendars.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the main point of contact between the company and the payroll vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the vendor to resolve any payroll discrepancies and ensure alignment with service level agreements (SLAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop positive relationships with payroll vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide responsive, accurate, and timely resolution for common payroll queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See opportunities for enhancing payroll processes and efficiencies in collaboration with the vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement best practices and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the Standard Operating Procedures manual is kept up to date with current payroll service provider model practices and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with vendor/3rd parties in relation to the processing of international assignees shadow payrolls and audit pay to ensure results agree with recommendations from mobility services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience of in house and/or managed service payroll within a large, complex international organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with EMEA payrolls, with an understanding of country-specific legislation, compliance requirements, and operational nuances&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good technical knowledge of statutory payments, pension/auto-enrolment, manual calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to input into and review change requests, collaborating across multiple teams and partners to obtain input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for providing exceptional quality service and striving for exceeding clients&#39; expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive anticipations of issues and developing collaborative relationships with upstream and downstream functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of general HR processes and data, including eligibility and procedures, to provide expected correct downstream pay result outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CIPP and/or equivalent qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expatriate processing experience and mobility understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary bonus opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid Working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dental Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On Site Gym&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised Café&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free soft drinks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On site bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to cycle garage and showers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
